<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cinca</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cinca is a river of Aragon in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> that rises in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> near Monte Perdido and flows south to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segre">Segre</a> shortly before that river meets the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a>. Its upper valley formed the medieval county of Sobrarbe, one of the cores of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon</a>, while its lower course crossed the plains once held by the Iberian Ilergetes.</p></div>
